  "explanation": {
    "en": "いつ means “when.” It is used to ask about time in general. Unlike specific times, いつ does not take に.\n\nKey points:\n• いつ = when (general)\n• Usually used without に\n• Often paired with verbs like 行きます, 来ます, 会います\n• For exact time, use time + に instead\n\nExample: “いつ行きますか” means “When will you go?” “いつ会いますか” means “When will we meet?”\n\nIf you want a specific time, answer with a time expression plus に: “三時に行きます.”\n\nPractice by asking simple questions: いつ帰りますか, いつ勉強しますか.",
    "ja": ""
  },
